Let $L(x)$ be the length of the segment joining the origin to the point $\big(x,f(x)\big)$. We use the distance formula to compute $L(x)$:

$\begin{align}
L(x)&=\sqrt{(x-0)^2+\big(f(x)-0\big)^2}
\\\\
&=\sqrt{x^2+(2x-3)^2}
\\\\
&=\sqrt{x^2+4x^2-12x+9}
\\\\
&=\sqrt{5x^2-12x+9}
\end{align}$
